# Testing rules

- Prefer fast unit tests first.
- Add integration tests when behavior depends on Spring context, database access, or serialization.
- For controller tests, prefer MockMvc unless the repo standardizes differently.
- For database integration, prefer Testcontainers over brittle local assumptions.
- Avoid mocking what you do not own when a slice or integration test is more truthful.
- Test happy path, validation failures, and one important edge case at minimum.
- Do not remove tests to make builds pass.
